Another subtlety — `this.draggedItem?.classList.add(...)` in rAF: if the drag already ended (super fast), draggedItem is null → skip. If a NEW drag started, draggedItem = new item → adds class — correct.

Hmm — wait, another consideration on `dragLeave`: `event.relatedTarget` during dragleave may be an element in the SAME container (child-to-child moves fire dragleave too). `container.contains(relatedTarget)` → skip. ✓. When relatedTarget is null (leaving window): contains(null) false → remove highlight. ✓

One more: `#hoveredContainer` checks `this.draggedItem` — so dragover/dragleave/drop from native non-card drags (files) are ignored. ✓ But hmm — dragLeave fires after drop? Order on successful drop: dragleave doesn't fire for the dropped element... drop → dragend. ✓

What about `drop` firing on the CARD ITSELF (dropping a card onto another card inside a container)? `event.target.closest(container)` finds the enclosing container → drop into that container. ✓ desired.

What about dropping into the SOURCE container — skip move; just reset. ✓ (no-op within one column)

Now — hmm, wait: one more edge. The `drop` event: `this.#hoveredContainer(event)` requires `this.draggedItem`. On drop we then `#reset()`. ✓.

